<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Will a firmware update change my hearing aid prescription?</h3>
<p>Typically no. Firmware updates usually preserve your fitting targets (gain and compression) set by your audiologist. They may reset user-level preferences (manual programs, button functions). If the update adds a new processing mode, your audiologist might create or fine-tune a program so you benefit from it.</p>

<h3>How often should I check for hearing aid updates?</h3>
<p>A practical rhythm is every 1–3 months, or whenever you notice problems (dropouts, charging quirks) or update your phone’s OS. Many apps notify you automatically. For major updates, ask your audiologist if they recommend installing right away or waiting a week.</p>

<h3>Can updates drain my battery faster?</h3>
<p>Most aim to maintain or improve battery life. After installing, compare a couple of similar days. If you see a consistent drop (more than a few percent), check app permissions and background settings first, then contact your audiologist or manufacturer support.</p>

<h3>What if a firmware update fails mid-way?</h3>
<p>Stay calm. Charge the aids, reboot your phone, power-cycle the aids, and try again next to the charger with solid Wi‑Fi. If it still fails, remove and re-pair the aids in both Bluetooth settings and the app. Your audiologist can usually complete the update in-clinic with fitting software.</p>


